# Frontend

Shell constraints: [architecture.mdc](./architecture.mdc). Design overlay for generic UI skills: [ui-design](../skills/ui-design/SKILL.md).

## Stack

- React 19 + Next.js App Router (client components for classroom data)
- Tailwind 4 + shadcn (`@base-ui/react`)
- Icons: **Lucide** — do not swap libraries
- Motion: Framer Motion (already in repo)

## Design tokens

Per `docs/PROJECT_SCOPE.md` §12:

- Brand sky: `#4ba3e8` (`--color-brand`)
- Accent pink: `#efa3bc` (`--color-accent-pink`)
- Page background: `#f7fafd`
- Cute, playful, gamified classroom — not corporate admin

## State and data

- Classroom data: `useAppData()` / `AppDataProvider` only — no TanStack Query, SWR, Zustand, or Redux for classroom JSON
- Local `useState` → lift to common ancestor → context when needed
- Derive values during render; avoid `useEffect` to sync derived state
- Do not define components inside render (remounts break focus/state)
- Keep existing `forwardRef`; memo/`useCallback`/`next/dynamic` only with profiler or bundle evidence

## Reuse before creating

- `src/components/classroom/*`, `components/ui/*`, existing `src/app/` page patterns

## Security

- No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` or DOM HTML sinks with student/teacher names or user text
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for animations

## Touch targets

- Classroom actions (+1, spin, pick student): 44px minimum where practical

## Dialogs

CRUD/scoring: `useModalFocusTrap` + `role="dialog"` + `aria-modal` + labelled heading (`gift-redeem-dialog.tsx`). Stacked modals: `modalTrapStack`. Full-screen shell overlays: `createPortal(..., document.body)`. Leave Lucky Wheel and sibling game modals without keyboard trap unless requested.
